The
```c
    int needed = frames_needed(p);
    int read = MPMIN(needed, frame_size);
```
bit was a bit interesting as the first function's comment notes that it returns "number of frames", yet `frame_size` clearly sounds like the size of a single frame. I will interpret this that `total_fill` will be the amount of data required for the amount of frames still required to be filled (per channel).
